  "evidencia": "Page: Even (band). Sentence: Even are an Australian indie rock three-piece fronted by singer-songwriter-guitarist, Ash Naylor, with Matthew Cotter on drums and Wally Kempton (also known as Wally Meanie) on bass guitar and backing vocals.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They formed in March 1994 and played regularly around the live music scene and toured both nationally and internationally.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They have released six studio albums, \"Less Is More\" (10 June 1996), \"Come Again\" (28 September 1998), \"A Different High\" (14 May 2001), \"Free Kicks\" (6 June 2004), \"Even\" (29 March 2008) and \"In Another Time\" (9 December 2011).\nPage: Incubus (band). Sentence: Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.\nPage: Ashley Naylor. Sentence: Ashley Naylor is an Australian musician, best known for his guitar and vocals in Melbourne-based band Even.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Even (band). Sentence: Even are an Australian indie rock three-piece fronted by singer-songwriter-guitarist, Ash Naylor, with Matthew Cotter on drums and Wally Kempton (also known as Wally Meanie) on bass guitar and backing vocals.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They formed in March 1994 and played regularly around the live music scene and toured both nationally and internationally.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They have released six studio albums, \"Less Is More\" (10 June 1996), \"Come Again\" (28 September 1998), \"A Different High\" (14 May 2001), \"Free Kicks\" (6 June 2004), \"Even\" (29 March 2008) and \"In Another Time\" (9 December 2011).\nPage: Incubus (band). Sentence: Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.\nPage: Ashley Naylor. Sentence: Ashley Naylor is an Australian musician, best known for his guitar and vocals in Melbourne-based band Even.",
