        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "02be834f-b147-54a7-8411-cee5f5953b4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Even, Incubus\n- People: Ash Naylor, Ashley Naylor, Matthew Cotter, Wally Kempton, Wally Meanie\n- Places: Australia, Melbourne, Calabasas, California\n- Topics: indie rock, rock music, studio albums, touring\n\nFacts:\n- Even formed in March 1994 as an Australian indie rock three-piece.\n- Even is fronted by singer-songwriter-guitarist Ash Naylor, with Matthew Cotter on drums and Wally Kempton, also known as Wally Meanie, on bass guitar and backing vocals.\n- Even played regularly on the live music scene and toured nationally and internationally.\n- Even released the studio album \"Less Is More\" on 10 June 1996.\n- Even released the studio album \"Come Again\" on 28 September 1998.\n- Even released the studio album \"A Different High\" on 14 May 2001.\n- Even released the studio album \"Free Kicks\" on 6 June 2004.\n- Even released the self-titled studio album \"Even\" on 29 March 2008.\n- Even released the studio album \"In Another Time\" on 9 December 2011.\n- Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.\n- Ashley Naylor is an Australian musician best known for guitar and vocals in the Melbourne-based band Even.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
